Hi team,

Quick update on the Gemma 4 tool-calling issue.

Error
Any request with "tools" (opencode, agents) to http://172.20.1.126:1234 failed with:
"Error rendering prompt with jinja template: Cannot call something that is not a function: got UndefinedValue"
Plain chat worked fine.

Actual cause
LM Studio converts our JSON into Gemma's prompt format using a chat template. It renders templates with its own lightweight Jinja engine (minja), which doesn't support some functions used in Gemma 4's tool-calling section. So only requests with tools crashed. The model itself is fine.

Fix
I set up a small proxy on the same server: http://172.20.1.126:8088
No changes were made to the LM Studio setup or the loaded model.

How it works
1. The proxy renders Google's official Gemma 4 template with full Jinja2 (no bug).
2. It sends the finished prompt text to LM Studio's /v1/completions, which runs no template.
3. It converts Gemma's tool-call output back into standard OpenAI "tool_calls" JSON.
Tested: the request that used to fail now returns finish_reason "tool_calls" correctly.

What you need to do
For tool calling (opencode / agents), change your base URL from
http://172.20.1.126:1234/v1  →  http://172.20.1.126:8088/v1
The model name stays the same. Plain chat on :1234 still works as before.

Let me know if you see any issues.
